HST Office: HST Sheets reports a number outside a function's domain as #NUM! like the leading
spreadsheet application (owner decision 2026-11-13), while text and wrong-type arguments stay #VALUE!.

Upstream raises "invalid argument" (Err:502, shown as #VALUE! since
hst-sheets-excel-formula-conventions.patch) both for domain errors and for type errors. The domain
errors now raise the #NUM! error (FormulaError::IllegalFPOperation, ERROR.TYPE 6, written to .xlsx
as #NUM!) through the new ScInterpreter::PushNumError():
- sc interpr1.cxx: SQRT, ACOSH, ATANH, ACOTH, BITAND/BITOR/BITXOR/BITLSHIFT/BITRSHIFT, RANDBETWEEN.
- sc interpr2.cxx: LOG, LN, LOG10, CEILING/FLOOR with opposite signs (FLOOR(x;0) is #DIV/0!), DAY of
  an out-of-range serial, WEEKDAY/WEEKNUM return type, DATE before year 0, negative TIME, DATEDIF
  (start after end, unknown unit), NETWORKDAYS/WORKDAY.INTL date overflow, EASTERSUNDAY, ROUNDSIG,
  DDB, DB, VDB, PDURATION, RRI, RATE, IPMT, PPMT, CUMIPMT, CUMPRINC, EFFECT, NOMINAL, BASE, DECIMAL;
  MIRR without both a gain and a loss is #DIV/0!.
- sc interpr3.cxx: GAMMA, GAMMALN, FACT, COMBIN(A), PERMUT(ATIONA), FISHER, every distribution and
  inverse (NORM, LOGNORM, EXPON, T, F, CHISQ, WEIBULL, POISSON, HYPGEOM, BINOM, NEGBINOM, GAMMA, BETA,
  CRITBINOM, B), CONFIDENCE(.T), ZTEST sigma, TTEST tails/type, STANDARDIZE, HARMEAN, GEOMEAN,
  PERCENTILE, QUARTILE, PERCENTRANK, TRIMMEAN, SMALL/LARGE k out of range. Arrays of different size
  give #N/A (paired TTEST, CHITEST, PEARSON/CORREL/COVAR/RSQ, SLOPE/INTERCEPT/STEYX, FORECAST) and
  SKEW without spread #DIV/0!, as there.
- sc interpr4/5/7/8.cxx: DGET with several matches, GCD/LCM of a negative number, MINVERSE of a
  singular matrix, LOGEST with y <= 0, COLOR, FORECAST.ETS* aggregation, data completion, confidence
  level, statistic type and target before the timeline.
- sc addincol.cxx, scaddins analysis: an add-in that rejects an argument value (IllegalArgumentException:
  BESSEL negative order, HEX2DEC invalid digit, YEARFRAC/coupon basis or frequency, IM* invalid
  complex number, ...) gives #NUM!. The Analysis add-in reports text or a wrong type where a number is
  expected (holidays, MULTINOMIAL/SERIESSUM lists, COMPLEX suffix, CONVERT units) with a
  RuntimeException, which stays #VALUE!.
Unchanged (#VALUE! there too): VALUE, NUMBERVALUE, CHAR, UNICHAR, LEFT/MID/RIGHT/REPT/REPLACE/
SUBSTITUTE positions and counts, DATEVALUE, TIMEVALUE, ROMAN, ARABIC, FIXED, DOLLAR, CHOOSE,
SUBTOTAL/AGGREGATE function numbers, lookup/array shape errors, MDETERM/MINVERSE/MMULT shapes, MUNIT.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_sheets_num_errors.py, tests/runtime/check-sheets-excel-formula-conventions.py.
